  "note": "Municipal elections, 15 January 1927. Only Clifton and Dufferin were contested. Ballyholme, Castle and Princetown returned their members unopposed. One spoilt vote. The paper prints total poll 694 and polling strength 985 with 291 non-voters, but the votes recorded sum to 593; the printed totals are not entered."
